.TH "RECORD\-PREPROCESS\.JL" "" "June 2026" ""
.SH "NAME"
\fBrecord\-preprocess\.jl\fR
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBrecord\-preprocess\.jl\fR [\fIoptions\fR] \fB\-\-\fR \fIcommand\fR [\fIarg\fR\|\.\|\.\|\.]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBrecord\-preprocess\.jl\fR parses a command invocation and generates the provenance boilerplate needed to record it in the RECORD workflow system\. It is intended to wrap an existing command call: everything before \fB\-\-\fR is interpreted as options to the preprocessor itself; everything after \fB\-\-\fR is the target command and its arguments\.
.P
The script produces two kinds of output:
.IP "1." 4
\fBStandard output\fR \(em a shell fragment assigning \fB$ARGS\fR with \fB\-\-record\-argument\-*\fR and \fB\-\-record\-stdout\-*\fR / \fB\-\-record\-stderr\-*\fR lines, one per argument or redirection, for direct inclusion in the provenance\-recording call\.
.IP "2." 4
\fBArgument\-types library file\fR (\fBlib\.<PROG>\.argument\-types\.sh\fR by default) \(em a shell script that registers each argument type with \fBrecord_argument_type\fR, with placeholder descriptions and ranges derived from the observed values\.
.IP "3." 4
\fBOutput\-types library file\fR (\fBlib\.<PROG>\.output\-types\.sh\fR by default) \(em a shell script that registers each redirected output with \fBrecord_output_box_type\fR\.
.IP "" 0
.P
The first token after \fB\-\-\fR must be a resolvable executable (\fBSys\.which\fR is used to verify this); it becomes \fB$PROG\fR and is used to namespace all generated identifiers\.
.P
Argument parsing of the passthrough section handles the three major command\-line conventions automatically:
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fB*NIX long options\fR (\fB\-\-flag\fR, \fB\-\-option=value\fR, \fB\-\-option value\fR)
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fB*NIX short options\fR (\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-o value\fR, \fB\-o=value\fR; with \fB\-U\fR, single\-hyphen strings are split into individual letter flags)
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBWindows/MSDOS switches\fR (\fB/S\fR, \fB/S:value\fR)
.IP "" 0
.P
Shell redirections (\fB>\fR, \fB>>\fR, \fB2>\fR, \fB2>>\fR, \fB2>&1\fR) are recognised in\-line and recorded as output types rather than arguments\.
.P
Ambiguities (e\.g\. whether a bare token following a flag is its value or an independent positional argument) are resolved heuristically by read\-ahead: if the next token starts with \fB\-\fR, \fB/\fR, or \fB>\fR it is treated as a new argument and the current token is classified as a flag\. Use \fB\-\-suppress\-alternatives\fR to silence the reporting of such ambiguities\.
.P
If \fB\-\-run\fR is supplied the target command is also executed under \fBstrace\fR, and the files it reads and writes are reported to standard output\.
.SH "OPTIONS"
Options must appear \fBbefore\fR \fB\-\-\fR\. Any positional argument before \fB\-\-\fR is an error\.
.TP
\fB\-a\fR \fIval\fR, \fB\-a=\fR\fIval\fR, \fB\-\-assignment\-operator\fR \fIval\fR, \fB\-\-assignment\-operator=\fR\fIval\fR
Override the character used as the assignment operator when splitting option names from values in the passthrough section\. By default the operator is inferred from context (\fB=\fR for long options, \fB:\fR for Windows switches, space otherwise)\.
.TP
\fB\-D\fR, \fB\-\-debug\fR
Enable debug logging to standard error via Julia's \fBLogging\fR module\.
.TP
\fB\-H\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print a usage summary including annotated output examples, then exit 0\.
.TP
\fB\-l\fR \fIval\fR, \fB\-l=\fR\fIval\fR, \fB\-\-argument\-types\-library\fR \fIval\fR, \fB\-\-argument\-types\-library=\fR\fIval\fR
Write the argument\-types shell fragment to \fIval\fR instead of the default path \fBlib\.<PROG>\.argument\-types\.sh\fR\.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR \fIval\fR, \fB\-o=\fR\fIval\fR, \fB\-\-output\-types\-library\fR \fIval\fR, \fB\-\-output\-types\-library=\fR\fIval\fR
Write the output\-types shell fragment to \fIval\fR instead of the default path \fBlib\.<PROG>\.output\-types\.sh\fR\.
.TP
\fB\-R\fR, \fB\-\-run\fR
Execute the passthrough command under \fBstrace\fR after generating the provenance fragments, and print the sets of files read and written\.
.TP
\fB\-S\fR, \fB\-\-suppress\-alternatives\fR
Do not report ambiguous argument assignments; silently accept the default interpretation\.
.TP
\fB\-U\fR, \fB\-\-unix\-flags\fR
Treat single\-hyphen options as compact flag strings (e\.g\. \fB\-ABC\fR is three flags \fB\-A\fR, \fB\-B\fR, \fB\-C\fR)\. Also sets \fB=\fR as the assignment operator for long options\.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print the version string and exit 0\.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Returns 0 on success\.
.P
Returns 2 (via \fBdie\fR) if:
.IP "\(bu" 4
a required value is missing for a recognised option;
.IP "\(bu" 4
an unrecognised option appears before \fB\-\-\fR;
.IP "\(bu" 4
a positional argument appears before \fB\-\-\fR;
.IP "\(bu" 4
the first passthrough token is not a resolvable executable; or
.IP "\(bu" 4
any other fatal error is detected during argument processing\.
.IP "" 0
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
\fBrecord\-preprocess\.jl\fR does not read any environment variables directly\. If \fB\-\-run\fR is used, the child process inherits the full environment\.
.SH "RETURN VALUE"
On success the script writes to three destinations:
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBstdout\fR: the \fB$ARGS\fR shell fragment\.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fB\fBlib\.<PROG>\.argument\-types\.sh\fR\fR (or the path given by \fB\-l\fR): the argument\-type registration script, opened in append mode\.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fB\fBlib\.<PROG>\.output\-types\.sh\fR\fR (or the path given by \fB\-o\fR): the output\-type registration script, opened in append mode\.
.IP "" 0
.SH "EXAMPLES"
Generate provenance fragments for a Python script invocation:
.IP "" 4
.nf
record\-preprocess\.jl \-\- prog\.py \e
    \-\-out\-file=dougs\.file \e
    \-on\-flag \e
    \-A \e
    \-i input_path\.dat \e
    "pickling times are fun times" \e
    2>&1 \e
    > dougs\.out
.fi
.IP "" 0
.P
Generate fragments using Unix flag mode and a custom argument\-types path:
.IP "" 4
.nf
record\-preprocess\.jl \e
    \-U \e
    \-l lib\.my_tool\.args\.sh \e
    \-\- my_tool \-Dvf input\.dat > output\.dat
.fi
.IP "" 0
.P
Generate fragments and also run the command, tracing file I/O:
.IP "" 4
.nf
record\-preprocess\.jl \-R \-\- my_tool \-\-config=conf\.yaml input\.dat
.fi
.IP "" 0
.SH "FILES"
.TP
\fBlib\.<PROG>\.argument\-types\.sh\fR
Shell script registering each argument type via \fBrecord_argument_type\fR\. Created or appended to in the current working directory unless overridden with \fB\-l\fR\.
.TP
\fBlib\.<PROG>\.output\-types\.sh\fR
Shell script registering each output type via \fBrecord_output_box_type\fR\. Created or appended to in the current working directory unless overridden with \fB\-o\fR\.
